      "body": "uptake_Ar (Ar) = 2.16 cm3/g at 1.013 bar"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "basic_NH2_groups → qst"
    },
    {
      "title": "Mechanism",
      "body": "absence_of_NH2_groups → qst"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] incorporate basic -NH2 groups into the Zn-based framework linker set, as in Zn-DAT using 3,5-diaminotriazole → CO2 heat of adsorption increases by about 8 kJ mol−1, from 31.7 to 39.5 kJ mol−1"
    },
    {
      "title": "Design Rule",
      "body": "[positive] combine Lewis acidic Zn(II) sites with basic -NH2 groups in Zn-DAT → enables selective CO2 adsorption and supports CO2 conversion to cyclic carbonates under mild conditions"
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparison",
      "body": "Zn-DAT vs Zn-TAZ: winner=subject_a on CO2_heat_of_adsorption_Qst"
    }
  ],
